## Hooking into Pytest's Failure Reporting

```python
# conftest.py
import pytest

@pytest.hookimpl(tryfirst=True, hookwrapper=True)
def pytest_runtest_makereport(item, call):
    outcome = yield
    rep = outcome.get_result()
    setattr(item, f"rep_{rep.when}", rep)

@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)
def screenshot_on_failure(request, driver):
    yield
    if request.node.rep_call.failed:
        driver.save_screenshot(f"failures/{request.node.name}.png")
```

This pattern (a pytest hook plus an `autouse` fixture) captures a screenshot **automatically** for every failing UI test, with zero extra code needed in the test functions themselves — set it up once in `conftest.py` and every future UI test benefits.

